<p>------------------------------------------------------------  </p>
<p>QUESTION OF THE WEEK: Economists were asked for their forecasts of three of the major economic parameters of the 1996/97 budget, namely GDP-A, CPI and employment growth all of which are expressed in year-average terms.</p>
<p>Analysts generally expected the government to estimate GDP-A in a 3.0 to 3.5 percent range, with most looking for 3.25 percent.  </p>
<p>They also expected the government to estimate CPI at around 2.0 percent, but were less sure on employment with many expecting the government to err on the side of optimism at 1.5-2.0 percent.</p>
